WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:04.046
You've witnessed miracles,
blood drinking,

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.381
and saw much fire.

00:00:06.465 --> 00:00:09.301
Let's answer
some burning questions.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:11.345
Here is everything
you need to know

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:13.096
about Midnight Mass.

00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:18.852
That wasn't an angel,
was it?

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.605
No.
It really, really wasn't.

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:27.736
What Monsignor Pruitt found
in that cave in the desert

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:28.946
was an all-out

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.990
Nosferatu-style
vampire creature

00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:33.492
with bonus wings.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:34.993
While he genuinely

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:37.079
initially saw it
as a saviour,

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:40.707
this was, in fact,
an ancient vampiric being

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.376
hiding in the shadows.

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:44.962
As showrunner Mike Flanagan
was growing up,

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.339
he was learning
about communion wine

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:49.842
at the same time
as getting into horror

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:51.969
and he saw direct parallels

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.054
between drinking the blood
of Jesus

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:57.182
and what he was reading
in Bram Stoker's Dracula.

00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:58.100
This is where

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.143
this particular monster
comes from.

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:02.604
And Midnight Mass'
executive producer,

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.566
Trevor Macy, has explained
that this creature

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:08.151
actually has
very basic needs.

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:12.364
It eats, it seeks shelter,
and it has enough brains

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.575
to not just murder
the Monsignor,

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:17.703
but let him take him back
to Crockett Island.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.539
But to fully explain
what happened here,

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:23.166
it's important
to talk about blood.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.003
In vampire lore,
in order for a human

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.880
to transform
into a bloodsucker,

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:29.631
the monster
must feed on you,

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:32.009
and then, as life drains
from your body,

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.761
they force
you to drink their blood.

00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:38.307
The consumption
of vampire blood is key.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.476
This then creates
a fully-fledged vampire

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.936
and this transformation

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.398
is what we see take place
violently in the church

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:49.067
as the congregation
come back to life

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:51.320
with that tell-tale light
in their eyes.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.949
As we all know,

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.618
on top of
an insatiable desire

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:58.619
for blood,

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:01.205
vampires
have an aversion to sunlight

00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:03.332
as it literally
cooks them alive.

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:04.708
And, of course,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.002
despite this one
looking pretty crusty,

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.046
they also have eternal youth

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.131
and the power
of fast healing.

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:15.385
Why was Monsignor Pruitt

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:18.180
able to go out
in the sunshine initially?

00:02:18.263 --> 00:02:20.307
This is a great question.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.518
If he'd been transformed
into a vampire,

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:25.771
how could Monsignor Pruitt
wonder around in the sun

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:28.148
when he initially arrives
on Crockett Island?

00:02:28.232 --> 00:02:29.775
Well, it turns out

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:31.818
that the monster
didn't kill him

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:32.819
in that cave.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:35.030
Despite the transfusion
of vampire blood

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:37.324
making him young again,
and taking him back

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.201
to the best version
of himself,

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:42.204
he was still human
and could, therefore,

00:02:42.287 --> 00:02:45.457
transport the monster
in a box to the island.

00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:46.458
It is only after

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:48.752
further consumption
of vampire blood

00:02:48.836 --> 00:02:51.839
that Monsignor Pruitt
eventually succumbs,

00:02:51.922 --> 00:02:53.382
as we see him die

00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:55.133
on the floor
of his own home.

00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:56.885
It's from this moment

00:02:56.969 --> 00:02:59.096
that he becomes
a full-on vampire.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:02.224
Which means the switch
over to nighttime ceremonies

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:03.517
from here on out.

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:07.938
Why did everyone
in the congregation

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.022
resurrect?

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:10.566
Unbeknownst to them,

00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:13.235
the entire congregation
of Crockett Island

00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:15.445
has been swigging
vampire blood

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:16.363
from the moment

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:18.615
that the Monsignor
returned to the island.

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:19.783
It turns out

00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:22.077
that he's been lacing
the communion wine

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:22.995
with the stuff,

00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:26.123
meaning he's been gradually
infecting the church-goers

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.207
with the blood.

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:29.459
Early on,
we catch a glimpse of him

00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:31.712
tipping a hip flask
into the wine

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:33.797
before the altar boys
take it out.

00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:37.217
Later on, we then see,
at the same time as Riley,

00:03:37.301 --> 00:03:39.720
that the creature
has been opening a vein

00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:43.265
and bleeding directly
into the communion wine.

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:44.975
Mmm, delicious.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.185
This means

00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:49.563
that everyone has gradually
been consuming the creature

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:51.607
and evolving
in a similar way

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.691
to the Monsignor.

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:55.611
This is why the members
of the congregation

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.821
have been so ready
to dance again

00:03:57.905 --> 00:04:00.532
and even
no longer need glasses.

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:02.743
It also fully explains

00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:05.204
the early miracle
of Leeza Scarborough

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:07.539
regaining
the use of her legs.

00:04:07.623 --> 00:04:10.292
Despite being shot
in the spine by Joe,

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:12.544
the consumption
of vampire blood

00:04:12.628 --> 00:04:14.838
gives her the power
to walk again.

00:04:14.922 --> 00:04:16.965
Vampires are hunters.

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:20.135
They require speed,
strength, and agility.

00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:22.471
When Monsignor Pruitt says

00:04:22.554 --> 00:04:24.431
he's the best version
of himself,

00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:27.392
that's what everyone else
is gradually becoming.

00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:29.436
This means
that when everyone dies,

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.688
they have
enough vampire in them

00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:33.357
that they will resurrect.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.816
And it doesn't
seem to matter

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.318
how you die either.

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:38.779
Whether it's shooting...

00:04:38.862 --> 00:04:39.738
throat slitting...

00:04:41.865 --> 00:04:44.034
or the Jonestown-like
mass poisoning,

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.745
if you've had the communion
wine at some point,

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:49.915
you'll come back with
a serious thirst for gore.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.044
It is worth noting, though,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.380
that Riley was turned
by the monster

00:04:56.463 --> 00:04:57.506
when he was killed,

00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:59.758
as he hadn't been drinking
the communion wine.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.470
How did Erin lose her baby?

00:05:03.554 --> 00:05:06.306
Erin losing her baby
is directly correlated

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.226
to the consumption
of the vampire blood.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.811
Sarah's
scientific conclusions

00:05:10.894 --> 00:05:13.438
about the infection
riding the body of the baby

00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:15.065
is absolutely right.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.818
Vampire,
in essence, are dead.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.737
They don't give life
and they don't procreate.

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:23.115
They consume
and consume only.

00:05:23.198 --> 00:05:25.075
Unless
you're watching Twilight,

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:28.036
babies
and vampires don't mix.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.622
The idea of the baby
just disappearing, though,

00:05:30.706 --> 00:05:31.999
is particularly unique.

00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:33.458
And Erin's test results,

00:05:33.542 --> 00:05:36.044
showing that there was never
any baby at all,

00:05:36.128 --> 00:05:38.297
means that her blood results
at that point,

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.464
are still normal,

00:05:39.548 --> 00:05:41.216
even if, clearly,

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.093
they didn't put it
in direct sunlight,

00:05:43.177 --> 00:05:44.344
like Sarah.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.310
Fucking bonkers.

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:54.396
Why did so many people
turn evil?

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:56.899
Once half the congregation
of Crockett Island

00:05:56.982 --> 00:05:58.650
resurrects in the church,

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.861
they turn
on the still human half,

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:03.739
treating them
like Bic Macs on legs.

00:06:03.822 --> 00:06:05.616
And this is before
they're unleashed

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:07.284
upon the rest of the island.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.745
But we have already seen

00:06:09.828 --> 00:06:12.539
that Riley could still make
important decisions,

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:13.916
choosing to die

00:06:13.999 --> 00:06:17.169
instead of facing his future
as a blood hungry monster.

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:19.588
And with
the Monsignor's help,

00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:22.216
he fights against
his initial urges,

00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:25.260
even the Monsignor
manages to fight his hunger.

00:06:25.344 --> 00:06:26.929
In the incident with Joe,

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:28.847
he manages
to convince himself

00:06:28.931 --> 00:06:30.307
it's God's message.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.559
Riley's parents,
Annie and Ed,

00:06:32.643 --> 00:06:35.020
also retain
complete control.

00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:38.398
I'm starving too, but...

00:06:38.482 --> 00:06:40.150
I didn't.

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:43.445
So, the congregation
do have the choice,

00:06:43.529 --> 00:06:45.405
but they give in
to their hunger,

00:06:45.489 --> 00:06:47.449
immediately becoming the mob

00:06:47.533 --> 00:06:50.661
and consumed with the idea
of being saved.

00:06:50.744 --> 00:06:53.455
Before he realises
the error of his ways,

00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:55.916
the Monsignor
has them so convinced

00:06:55.999 --> 00:06:57.417
that they
are the army of God,

00:06:57.501 --> 00:07:00.045
that they succumb
to mob rule.

00:07:00.128 --> 00:07:02.756
The right-wing
conspiracy theorist subtext

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.091
is strong here

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:06.176
as they slaughter
their family members

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.553
and drink their blood.

00:07:07.636 --> 00:07:09.596
Only stopping with regret

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.598
when the truth,
quite literally,

00:07:11.682 --> 00:07:12.558
dawns on them.

00:07:12.641 --> 00:07:15.769
I don't know,
but I think I killed my mom.

00:07:15.853 --> 00:07:17.896
Why didn't the Monsignor die

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.815
when he got shot
in the head?

00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:22.067
Vampires aren't zombies.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.404
It did take the Monsignor
a little while to resurrect

00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:26.989
after he was shot
in the skull,

00:07:27.072 --> 00:07:28.907
but even
a bullet to the brain

00:07:28.991 --> 00:07:30.492
can't stop a vampire.

00:07:34.246 --> 00:07:36.582
We never see
the old-fashioned garlic

00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:39.334
or stakes being tried,
but the ancient vampire

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:42.045
is happy to wear
a religious robe

00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:43.463
and walk in a church.

00:07:43.547 --> 00:07:44.923
What we do see, though,

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:47.467
is that
the Monsignor's hand bleeds

00:07:47.551 --> 00:07:48.802
when he holds a Rosary.

00:07:48.886 --> 00:07:50.470
So, perhaps, this vampire

00:07:50.554 --> 00:07:53.182
does have some more
stereotypical aspects.

00:07:53.265 --> 00:07:57.144
Namely, a serious allergy
to touching crosses.

00:07:57.227 --> 00:08:00.314
What was the relationship
between Monsignor Pruitt

00:08:00.397 --> 00:08:01.690
and Sarah's mother?

00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:04.026
It was a bit
of a late game reveal,

00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:07.237
but it turns out that Sarah
is the illegitimate child

00:08:07.321 --> 00:08:09.448
of the Monsignor
and her mother.

00:08:09.531 --> 00:08:10.407
The reason

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.492
that the Monsignor
passionately made sure

00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:15.370
he was giving her mother
the communion wine every day

00:08:15.454 --> 00:08:18.582
was to restore the woman
he loved so much.

00:08:18.665 --> 00:08:22.169
This cures her dementia
and gradually de-ages her,

00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:25.088
making her look even younger
than her daughter.

00:08:25.172 --> 00:08:27.549
A conversation
on the step of the church

00:08:27.633 --> 00:08:29.593
reveals that Sarah
is their daughter

00:08:29.676 --> 00:08:32.638
and that their lives could
never have been entwined

00:08:32.721 --> 00:08:35.015
even if he had
left the church for her.

00:08:35.098 --> 00:08:37.309
It's another
devasting reveal,

00:08:37.392 --> 00:08:40.187
especially
as the Monsignor professes

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.855
how proud he is of Sarah

00:08:41.939 --> 00:08:44.191
as she attempts
to destroy the church.

00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:46.360
No, I've so proud of you
and I just wish,

00:08:46.443 --> 00:08:47.986
I just wish that...

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.072
that we had gotten
to know each other.

00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:53.992
Why could Leeza no longer
feel her legs at the end?

00:08:54.076 --> 00:08:55.786
Leeza's sudden realisation

00:08:55.869 --> 00:08:57.621
that she's
once again paralysed,

00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:59.581
also might
answer the question

00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:02.251
as to whether the creature
managed to fly away.

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:04.253
As Crockett Island burns

00:09:04.336 --> 00:09:06.338
and its inhabitants
are incinerated

00:09:06.421 --> 00:09:07.714
by the morning sun,

00:09:07.798 --> 00:09:09.842
Leeza being paralysed
one more

00:09:09.925 --> 00:09:12.761
is an indication
that the spell is broken.

00:09:12.845 --> 00:09:14.179
I can't feel my legs.

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:16.974
The power of the blood
has been eradicated.

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:19.643
She is no longer
a vampire in waiting

00:09:19.726 --> 00:09:21.603
and is a mere human again.

00:09:21.687 --> 00:09:23.689
The irony is heart breaking,

00:09:23.772 --> 00:09:25.983
but Leeza is no longer
going to become

00:09:26.066 --> 00:09:27.568
a creature of the night.

00:09:27.651 --> 00:09:29.778
The sun is rising
on a new day

00:09:29.862 --> 00:09:32.072
where the vampire
has not won.

00:09:32.155 --> 00:09:35.325
It also means
Erin's painful sacrifice

00:09:35.409 --> 00:09:36.660
was not in vain

00:09:36.743 --> 00:09:38.745
as she shredded
the creature's wings

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:40.205
with that knife.

00:09:40.289 --> 00:09:42.708
It might not feel
like a happy ending,

00:09:42.791 --> 00:09:44.918
but the survival
of Warren and Leeza

00:09:45.002 --> 00:09:47.004
and a lack
of the vampires' power,

00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:48.964
would suggest
that the nightmare

00:09:49.047 --> 00:09:50.591
is indeed over.

00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:54.344
So, hopefully,
that's all your questions

00:09:54.428 --> 00:09:55.721
from Midnight Mass answered.

00:09:55.804 --> 00:09:58.473
Let us know your theories
in the comments below

00:09:58.557 --> 00:10:01.727
and remember to subscribe
to Still Watching Netflix

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:02.811
for more deep dives

00:10:02.895 --> 00:10:05.022
into your favourite shows
and movies.

